From: openEuler RISC-V Packages contributors
Subject: Define IP arithmetic and bounded allocation; retain final text lines
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
Source: https://pc-tools.net/files/unix/grepcidr-2.0.tar.gz
Source-SHA256: 61886a377dabf98797145c31f6ba95e6837b6786e70c932324b7d6176d50f7fb
Applies-to: grepcidr 2.0, grepcidr.c and Makefile
Upstream-status: package-local; no upstream issue, comment or PR created

Root cause (static review, not an observed crash/CVE): unsigned-char IPv4
octets promoted to signed int before left shift; signed 1<<31 masks; ctype
arguments may be negative char; array/line growth lacks checked size and a
temporary realloc pointer. A final 511/1023/... byte line without newline
can be discarded after expansion when the following read reaches EOF.

Use unsigned arithmetic/ctype bytes, checked growth and int-sized fgets
chunks, and accept accumulated data only on EOF (not a partial read error).
Recognize the legal all-zero IPv6 token through the existing inet_pton
validation. Honor caller LDFLAGS. Retain all options/features/default algorithm
with narrow edge fixes, original -O3/-Wall/-Werror, supplied manual and doc target.
Original notices are snapshotted before applying this patch. No source
execution, fault injection or general security/performance claim follows.

Removal: re-review a fixed official release addressing these exact cases
and pass the same target CLI vectors before dropping this owned patch.

